{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"- **Written policies:** Adopt and implement basket construction/acceptance procedures in the ETF’s and shareholders’ best interests.\n- **Custom-basket controls:** Set detailed construction/acceptance parameters, processes for revisions/deviations, and adviser-employee titles/roles responsible for reviewing each custom basket’s compliance. Rule 38a-1 requires board-approved compliance policies, CCO oversight and annual review—not board approval of individual baskets.\n- **Records:** Retain written authorized-participant agreements and, for each exchanged basket, holding identifiers, quantities, cash-balancing amounts and AP identity. For custom baskets, retain the designation and a statement of compliance with custom-basket policies. Keep records five years, the first two easily accessible.\n- **Worth knowing:** A custom basket is non-representative or representative but different from that business day’s initial basket. “Non-standard order” is an operational/commercial label, not a Rule 6c-11 category; unusual timing or processing alone does not make a basket custom."}}
